IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch23-32`

-- Tests for chapters 23 to 32.  Every expected value was written from the text before the
-- file was run; unit ids (23.1, 26.4 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").
-- The dates in the chapter 32 tests are arbitrary; the text names no calendar and no year.

§ `Tests -- chapters 23 to 32`

§§ `Chapter 23 -- bridges`

-- 23.1: "except those who from of old were legally bound to do so".
#ASSERT `ch 23 -- a community or individual may be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank` TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 23 -- a community or individual may be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank` FALSE EQUALS Barred

§§ `Chapter 24 -- pleas of the Crown`

-- 24.1: "No sheriff, constable, coroners, or others of our bailiffs".
#ASSERT `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` `a sheriff` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` `a constable` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` `a coroner` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` `a bailiff` EQUALS Barred
-- The King and the chief justiciar are not named in 24.1.
#ASSERT `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` `the King` EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` `the King's chief justiciar` EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 24 -- no sheriff, constable, coroner or other bailiff shall hold pleas of the Crown` `a sheriff` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a sheriff` DOES `hold pleas of the Crown` AT 5
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 24 -- no sheriff, constable, coroner or other bailiff shall hold pleas of the Crown` `a coroner` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a coroner` DOES `hold pleas of the Crown` AT 5
-- expect: MUST NOT `hold pleas of the Crown`
#TRACE `ch 24 -- no sheriff, constable, coroner or other bailiff shall hold pleas of the Crown` `a constable` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 24 -- no sheriff, constable, coroner or other bailiff shall hold pleas of the Crown` `the King` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `hold pleas of the Crown` AT 5

§§ `Chapter 25 -- the old rents`

-- 25.1: arguments are unit, the old rent, the rent demanded, an additional payment demanded.
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a county` 100 100 FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a county` 100 101 FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a county` 100 100 TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a hundred` 50 51 FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a wapentake` 50 51 FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a trithing` 50 50 TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a trithing` 50 50 FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- Fork F25: a rent below the old rent is not an increase; "shall remain at the old rents" is not an if, unless or only, so the text does not say it is allowed (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a hundred` 50 49 FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- "(except our demesne manors)".
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a demesne manor` 100 200 TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `a demesne manor` 100 200 TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `some other unit` 100 200 TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 26 -- the chattels of a deceased debtor of the Crown`

-- 26.1: arguments are officer, a holder of a lay fief of the King has died, letters patent exhibited, chattels found upon the lay fief, value to be attached, debt owed to the King, done at the sight of lawful men.
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a bailiff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 50 TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- "to the value of that debt": one over is too much.
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 51 50 TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- "found upon the lay fief".
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE FALSE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- "at the sight of lawful men".
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- No letters patent exhibited, the holder alive, or an officer the text does not name.
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; now the text's no, because "our sheriff or bailiff shall exhibit our letters patent" is a limb of the text's own if, and he has not exhibited them.
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` TRUE FALSE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` FALSE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; now the text's no, because "If any one holding of us a lay fief shall die" is the other limb of the same if, and the holder is alive.
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a sheriff` FALSE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `a constable` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 26 -- the sheriff or bailiff may attach and catalogue chattels to the value of the debt` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a sheriff` DOES `attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased found upon the lay fief, to the value of the debt, at the sight of lawful men` AT 3
-- expect: MAY `attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased found upon the lay fief, to the value of the debt, at the sight of lawful men`
#TRACE `ch 26 -- the sheriff or bailiff may attach and catalogue chattels to the value of the debt` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 26 -- the sheriff or bailiff may attach and catalogue chattels to the value of the debt` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE TRUE 51 50 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 26.2: arguments are chattels have been attached, the debt which is evident has been fully paid.
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the attached chattels may be removed from the lay fief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the attached chattels may be removed from the lay fief` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the attached chattels may be removed from the lay fief` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- 26.3: arguments are the value of the chattels, the debt which is evident.
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the value of the residue left to the executors` 100 60 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the value of the residue left to the executors` 100 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the value of the residue left to the executors` 50 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the value of the residue left to the executors` 100 0 EQUALS 100
-- 26.4: arguments are nothing is due to the King, he leaves a wife or children.
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the wife and children have their reasonable shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the wife and children have their reasonable shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the wife and children have their reasonable shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 26 -- the wife and children have their reasonable shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`

§§ `Chapter 27 -- the chattels of a freeman who dies intestate`

#ASSERT `ch 27 -- how the chattels are distributed` TRUE EQUALS `By the hands of his nearest kinsfolk and friends, under the supervision of the church`
#ASSERT `ch 27 -- how the chattels are distributed` FALSE EQUALS `Distribution not covered`
-- expect: MUST `distribute the chattels of the freeman who died intestate`
#TRACE `ch 27 -- the nearest kinsfolk and friends shall distribute the chattels of a freeman who died intestate` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 27 -- the nearest kinsfolk and friends shall distribute the chattels of a freeman who died intestate` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the nearest kinsfolk and friends of the deceased` DOES `distribute the chattels of the freeman who died intestate` AT 20
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 27 -- the nearest kinsfolk and friends shall distribute the chattels of a freeman who died intestate` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- "saving to every one the debts which the deceased owed to him": arguments are died intestate, the deceased owed this person a debt.
#ASSERT `ch 27 -- the debt which the deceased owed to a person is saved to him` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 27 -- the debt which the deceased owed to a person is saved to him` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 27 -- the debt which the deceased owed to a person is saved to him` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 27 -- the debt which the deceased owed to a person is saved to him` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`

§§ `Chapter 28 -- corn and provisions`

-- 28.1: arguments are officer, he tenders money for it immediately, the seller permits postponement.
#ASSERT `ch 28 -- the officer may take corn or other provisions in this way` `a constable` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 28 -- the officer may take corn or other provisions in this way` `a bailiff` FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
-- Money tendered at once, no postponement: "without immediately tendering money" describes the barred taking, and "unless" governs only the postponement (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 28 -- the officer may take corn or other provisions in this way` `a constable` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 28 -- the officer may take corn or other provisions in this way` `a constable` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 28 -- the officer may take corn or other provisions in this way` `a sheriff` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 28 -- no constable or other bailiff shall take corn or other provisions without immediately tendering money` `a constable` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a constable` DOES `take corn or other provisions without immediately tendering money` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `take corn or other provisions without immediately tendering money`
#TRACE `ch 28 -- no constable or other bailiff shall take corn or other provisions without immediately tendering money` `a bailiff` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 28 -- no constable or other bailiff shall take corn or other provisions without immediately tendering money` `a constable` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a constable` DOES `take corn or other provisions without immediately tendering money` AT 2

§§ `Chapter 29 -- castle-guard`

-- 29.1: arguments are officer, the knight is willing to perform it himself, he cannot from a reasonable cause, another responsible man will perform it.
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the constable may compel the knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the constable may compel the knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
-- Not willing, and either cannot do it himself with no other responsible man, or can: the text does not say whether the constable may compel him here (not covered).
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the constable may compel the knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the constable may compel the knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the constable may compel the knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the constable may compel the knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a bailiff` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 29 -- no constable shall compel a knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a constable` DOES `compel a knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `compel a knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard`
#TRACE `ch 29 -- no constable shall compel a knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 29 -- no constable shall compel a knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `a constable` FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a constable` DOES `compel a knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` AT 2
-- 29.2: "if we have led or sent him upon military service, he shall be relieved from guard in proportion".
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the knight is relieved from guard in proportion to his time on service` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the knight is relieved from guard in proportion to his time on service` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the knight is relieved from guard in proportion to his time on service` FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
-- The text states no proportion, so the number of days of guard is not covered (fork F29).
#ASSERT `ch 29 -- the days of guard of which the knight is relieved` 30 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Chapter 30 -- horses and carts`

-- 30.1: arguments are the horses or carts belong to a freeman, he does not agree.
#ASSERT `ch 30 -- horses or carts may be taken for transport duty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 30 -- horses or carts may be taken for transport duty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 30 -- horses or carts may be taken for transport duty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 30 -- no sheriff or bailiff or other person shall take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a sheriff` DOES `take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will` AT 2
-- "or any other person".
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 30 -- no sheriff or bailiff or other person shall take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will` `any other person` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any other person` DOES `take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will`
#TRACE `ch 30 -- no sheriff or bailiff or other person shall take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will` `a bailiff` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 30 -- no sheriff or bailiff or other person shall take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will` `a bailiff` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a bailiff` DOES `take the horses or carts of a freeman for transport duty against his will` AT 2

§§ `Chapter 31 -- wood`

-- 31.1: arguments are taker, the wood is not the King's, the owner does not agree.
#ASSERT `ch 31 -- wood may be taken for the King's castles or other work` `the King` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 31 -- wood may be taken for the King's castles or other work` `a bailiff` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 31 -- wood may be taken for the King's castles or other work` `the King` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 31 -- wood may be taken for the King's castles or other work` `the King` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 31 -- wood may be taken for the King's castles or other work` `a sheriff` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 31 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall take wood which is not the King's against the will of the owner` `the King` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `take wood which is not the King's for the King's work, against the will of the owner` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `take wood which is not the King's for the King's work, against the will of the owner`
#TRACE `ch 31 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall take wood which is not the King's against the will of the owner` `a bailiff` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 31 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall take wood which is not the King's against the will of the owner` `a bailiff` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a bailiff` DOES `take wood which is not the King's for the King's work, against the will of the owner` AT 2

§§ `Chapter 32 -- the lands of persons convicted of felony`

-- 32.1: one year and one day from 15 January 2001 is 16 January 2002.
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the last day the King may retain the lands` (Date 15 1 2001) EQUALS Date 16 1 2002
-- A starting day of 29 February 2000: a year on is 28 February 2001 (the library clamps; fork F32b), and one day more is 1 March 2001.
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the last day the King may retain the lands` (Date 29 2 2000) EQUALS Date 1 3 2001
-- Arguments are the lands are those of a convicted person, the starting day, the day in question.
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the King may retain the lands on this day` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 16 1 2002) EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the King may retain the lands on this day` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 15 1 2002) EQUALS `Not barred`
-- "beyond one year and one day": the day after is too late.
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the King may retain the lands on this day` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 17 1 2002) EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the King may retain the lands on this day` FALSE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 17 1 2002) EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- "shall thereafter be handed over to the lords of the fiefs".
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the lands are handed over to the lords of the fiefs` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 17 1 2002) EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the lands are handed over to the lords of the fiefs` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 16 1 2002) EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 32 -- the lands are handed over to the lords of the fiefs` FALSE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 17 1 2002) EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 32 -- the King will not retain the lands beyond one year and one day` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 17 1 2002) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `retain the lands of a convicted felon beyond one year and one day` AT 2
-- expect: MUST NOT `retain the lands of a convicted felon beyond one year and one day`
#TRACE `ch 32 -- the King will not retain the lands beyond one year and one day` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 17 1 2002) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 32 -- the King will not retain the lands beyond one year and one day` TRUE (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 16 1 2002) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `retain the lands of a convicted felon beyond one year and one day` AT 2

-- assertions written: 72.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
